@dsh-external/dsh-web-skins README · ✨ How it works (why zero core changes)：- `ThemeService.register({ id, colorScheme, tokens })` is the **officially supported third-party theme surface** (the `--dsw-*` token system: static palette + alias semantic layer + specific component layer, dark palette under `body[data-ds-dark-theme]`); `ThemePresenter` projects a registered skin's tokens onto the body as inline variables and persists the preference in `dsh.theme`.
- This plugin bulk-registers every skin into `ThemeService` and registers a **Skins** row in the settings **General** section (reusing the official `settings.general.item` slot, same pattern as the built-in Appearance row).
- Image skins additionally maintain `body[data-ds-skin="<id>"]` plus one plugin-owned `<style>` tag (text replaced on skin switch, fully retracted on teardown); backgrounds are **inlined into the bundle as data URLs** — no external hosting.

@dsh-external/dsh-web-skins README · Skin discipline：- **Token-only first**: if a skin can be expressed with `--dsw-alias-*` overrides alone, write no CSS; any CSS must be scoped under `body[data-ds-skin="<id>"]` and fully replaced/retracted on skin switch.
- **Self-contained art**: backgrounds are inlined as data URLs — no external URLs, no hosting dependency; images are background atmosphere only, readability is guaranteed by the token layer (translucent base + opaque content layers).
- **Don't reinvent the wheel**: when you need more settings entries / skin preview thumbnails, check whether the official slot system covers it before hard-coding anything into this repo.

@dsh-external/dsh-web-skins README · 🌐 Bilingual-pairing gate (i18n)：- the content blob hash of each side (`sha1("blob <len>\0" + LF-normalized content)`), the anchor of the last confirmed-consistent state;
- a **structural-signature comparison**: heading depths, code blocks (verbatim), table dimensions, list shapes, and link targets must match between the sides — only prose may differ; the language switcher, `#` anchors, and `exemptLinks` (language-localized doc links) are skipped;
- `pnpm verify` runs this gate and `pnpm i18n` runs it alone; when editing either side of a doc, update the other together, then:

